## Stern + Gonzo On This Repo

The repo already manages Stern through the `stern_cli` role. Gonzo's upstream
Stern guide recommends JSON output so Gonzo can retain richer attributes during
analysis.

Good examples:

```bash
stern . --all-namespaces --output json | gonzo
stern . -n kube-system --output json | gonzo
stern . -n kube-system --tail 100 --output json | gonzo
stern "api-*" -n production --output json | gonzo
stern . -n production --since 1h --output json | gonzo
```

Stern guidance for Gonzo:

- Prefer `--output json` so Gonzo can populate attributes cleanly
- Use `--tail` or `--since` to keep large streams bounded
- Use a more specific pod pattern than `.` when performance matters

